{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532161960,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d273b791001VRHQAursgxJYDj","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","messageID":"msg_1d2738110001N97DJQRuDjJbBL","type":"tool","id":"call_4ada07d3f55a4205bab16653","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md, lines 1-222\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Ordered tasks to add the Gate 2 command bullet, copy it into the Cursor rule, hand hub modes to their commands, name the plan workflow at Gate 3 and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`. `CHK` is `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`. `HOOKDOC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`. `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `G1T` is `(cd $SSK/cli && npx vitest run tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .)`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12, and `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer. No task reads holdout prompt text.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0, 2 tasks: T001, T002. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-values.ts`), T007 (`advisor-observability.vitest.ts`), T008 (`hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`), T009, T010 and T011 (one `ROUTER.md` each), T012 (`spec-gate-core.mjs`), T013 (`create.sh`), T014 (the deriver, only if its condition holds).\n35: - Wave 2, 8 tasks: T015 (`render.ts`), T016 (`MAN`), T017 (gate1 test), T018 (`HOOKDOC`), T019 (parity test, new), T020 (spec-gate test), T021 (runtime-mirrors README), T022 (label removal test, new).\n36: - Wave 3, 4 tasks: T023 (child render test, new), T024 (`MAN`, generated), T025 (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, generated), T026 (`HOOKDOC`).\n37: - Verification, 9 tasks, one at a time: T027 to T035.\n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n43: ## Phase 1: Setup\n44: \n45: - [x] T001 Re-read the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$CHK | grep -E \"^A(4|6) |^STATUS\"` prints `44 current`, `15629 of 16384` and `STATUS=OK`, `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints `30 pins`, `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 and `node $S/measure-policies.mjs | head -1` prints `commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}`.\n46: - [x] T002 Confirm phase 005 shipped the brief line (`$S/phase005-check.txt`). Verify: `bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"create a readme for the utils folder\"` prints a line holding `/create:readme` and `(start)`. If it does not, mark T014, T015, T023, T026 and T033 `[B]` with the line it printed, and carry on with the rest.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n52: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n53: \n54: - [x] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55: - [x] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56: - [x] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false`, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57: - [x] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58: - [x] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59: - [x] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60: - [x] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61: - [x] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n62: - [x] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n63: - [x] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\n64: - [x] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\n65: - [x] T014 The command table phase 005 generates (`COMMAND_ROWS` in `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) carries a policy but no `mutating` class, and T015 needs the class. In `renderCommandRows` of `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, add `mutating: '<class>'` to each `COMMAND_ROWS` row, taken from the same `commandPolicies` record that supplies the row's policy, placed after `policy` and left out when the row has no policy record. In `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, add `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to the `CommandRow` interface, outside the generated block. Then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0 and `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n67: - [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68: - [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69: - [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70: - [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71: - [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72: - [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73: - [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n75: - [ ] T024 Regenerate the manifest's derived copy (`MAN`). Verify: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` exits 0, then `--check` prints `PASS: 44 sections, 31 pins, derived matches AGENTS.md`.\n76: - [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n83: ## Phase 3: Verification\n84: \n85: - [ ] T027 Run the agents-md check (`$S/after-check.txt`). Verify: `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK`, A4 `44 current`, A5 `31/31 pins hold`, A10 `6/6` and A6 at or under `16384`, expected `16092` with the T003 text unchanged.\n86: - [ ] T028 Run the rule-copy canary. Verify: `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/scripts/check-rule-copies.js | head -1` prints a line starting `OK: all rule invariants present`.\n87: - [ ] T029 Run the pointer test and check. Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed, and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T030 Run the spec gate test. Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T031 Run the advisor checks. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -n \"copilot\" $ADV --glob \"*.ts\" --glob \"!dist/**\" --glob \"!node_modules/**\"` prints only the new test and the adapter-path guards in `tests/hooks/settings-driven-invocation-parity.vitest.ts` and `stress-test/skill-advisor/hooks-parity-stress.vitest.ts` and `npm test` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T032 Run the three hub checks. Verify: `for h in sk-doc sk-design system-deep-loop; do node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/$h > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"$h exit=$?\"; done` prints `exit=0` three times.\n91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n92: - [ ] T034 Check scope and comment hygiene. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` names only files in `spec.md` section 3, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- '*.ts' '*.cjs' '*.mjs' '*.sh' | rg \"^\\+.*(REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|specs/|ADR-)\"` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T035 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n99: ## Completion Criteria\n100: \n101: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n102: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n103: - [ ] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 with the bullet in place\n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n109: ## Cross-References\n110: \n111: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n112: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n113: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n114: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md` R5, R6, R10b, L4, L5, L10, G1 and G3\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## Verification Checklist\n120: \n121: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n122: ## Verification Protocol\n123: \n124: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n125: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n126: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n127: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n128: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n129: \n130: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. An A6 reading above 16384 blocks the phase.\n131: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n136: ## Pre-Implementation\n137: \n138: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The four wording questions have an operator answer, quoted in `spec.md` section 10. Evidence: answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog. T003, T006, T012, T013, T015 and T026 follow those answers.\n139: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n140: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n146: ## Code Quality\n147: \n148: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] In `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `node --check` exits 0 on `SYNC` and `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n149: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n150: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n151: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n157: ## Testing Checklist\n158: \n159: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n160: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n161: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The child render test covers every renderer axis in `plan.md` (T023).\n162: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The spec gate test, the parity test and `npm test` in `$ADV` report 0 failed (T030, T031).\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n168: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n169: \n170: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: one rule, read by seven runtimes through four surfaces.\n171: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the pointer generator is checked: `rg -l \"sync-gate1-pointers\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists only files this phase changed or confirmed unchanged in `plan.md`.\n172: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` is checked: `rg -n \"GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists the core, its test and the injection contract, which names it without quoting it.\n173: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` are listed in the two test file headers.\n174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n175: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n181: ## Security\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] A child never sees a bare `start` or `ask` command line (T023).\n184: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No changed file names `/local-skilled-alignment`: `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n185: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The pointer block copies tracked `AGENTS.md` text only (T004).\n186: - [ ] CHK-033 [P0] A stored record carrying `copilot` is skipped by both readers without an error, and tool input carrying it is rejected (T022).\n187: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n192: ## Documentation\n193: \n194: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same bullet text, byte count and pin count.\n195: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] `HOOKDOC` names seven adapters and holds the invocation table (T005, T018).\n196: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The runtime-mirrors README names both pointer blocks (T021).\n197: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n198: \n199: ---\n200: \n201: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n202: ## File Organization\n203: \n204: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, before and after output live in `scratch/` only.\n205: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n206: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n211: ## Verification Summary\n212: \n213: | Category | Total | Verified |\n214: |----------|-------|----------|\n215: | P0 Items | 13 | 1/13 |\n216: | P1 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n217: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n218: \n219: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n221: \n222: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md, lines 1-222\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Ordered tasks to add the Gate 2 command bullet, copy it into the Cursor rule, hand hub modes to their commands, name the plan workflow at Gate 3 and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`. `CHK` is `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`. `HOOKDOC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`. `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `G1T` is `(cd $SSK/cli && npx vitest run tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .)`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12, and `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer. No task reads holdout prompt text.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0, 2 tasks: T001, T002. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-values.ts`), T007 (`advisor-observability.vitest.ts`), T008 (`hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`), T009, T010 and T011 (one `ROUTER.md` each), T012 (`spec-gate-core.mjs`), T013 (`create.sh`), T014 (the deriver, only if its condition holds).\n35: - Wave 2, 8 tasks: T015 (`render.ts`), T016 (`MAN`), T017 (gate1 test), T018 (`HOOKDOC`), T019 (parity test, new), T020 (spec-gate test), T021 (runtime-mirrors README), T022 (label removal test, new).\n36: - Wave 3, 4 tasks: T023 (child render test, new), T024 (`MAN`, generated), T025 (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, generated), T026 (`HOOKDOC`).\n37: - Verification, 9 tasks, one at a time: T027 to T035.\n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n43: ## Phase 1: Setup\n44: \n45: - [x] T001 Re-read the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$CHK | grep -E \"^A(4|6) |^STATUS\"` prints `44 current`, `15629 of 16384` and `STATUS=OK`, `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints `30 pins`, `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 and `node $S/measure-policies.mjs | head -1` prints `commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}`.\n46: - [x] T002 Confirm phase 005 shipped the brief line (`$S/phase005-check.txt`). Verify: `bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"create a readme for the utils folder\"` prints a line holding `/create:readme` and `(start)`. If it does not, mark T014, T015, T023, T026 and T033 `[B]` with the line it printed, and carry on with the rest.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n52: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n53: \n54: - [x] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55: - [x] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56: - [x] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false`, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57: - [x] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58: - [x] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59: - [x] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60: - [x] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61: - [x] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n62: - [x] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n63: - [x] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\n64: - [x] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\n65: - [x] T014 The command table phase 005 generates (`COMMAND_ROWS` in `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) carries a policy but no `mutating` class, and T015 needs the class. In `renderCommandRows` of `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, add `mutating: '<class>'` to each `COMMAND_ROWS` row, taken from the same `commandPolicies` record that supplies the row's policy, placed after `policy` and left out when the row has no policy record. In `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, add `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to the `CommandRow` interface, outside the generated block. Then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0 and `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n67: - [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68: - [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69: - [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70: - [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71: - [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72: - [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73: - [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n75: - [ ] T024 Regenerate the manifest's derived copy (`MAN`). Verify: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` exits 0, then `--check` prints `PASS: 44 sections, 31 pins, derived matches AGENTS.md`.\n76: - [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n83: ## Phase 3: Verification\n84: \n85: - [ ] T027 Run the agents-md check (`$S/after-check.txt`). Verify: `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK`, A4 `44 current`, A5 `31/31 pins hold`, A10 `6/6` and A6 at or under `16384`, expected `16092` with the T003 text unchanged.\n86: - [ ] T028 Run the rule-copy canary. Verify: `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/scripts/check-rule-copies.js | head -1` prints a line starting `OK: all rule invariants present`.\n87: - [ ] T029 Run the pointer test and check. Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed, and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T030 Run the spec gate test. Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T031 Run the advisor checks. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -n \"copilot\" $ADV --glob \"*.ts\" --glob \"!dist/**\" --glob \"!node_modules/**\"` prints only the new test and the adapter-path guards in `tests/hooks/settings-driven-invocation-parity.vitest.ts` and `stress-test/skill-advisor/hooks-parity-stress.vitest.ts` and `npm test` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T032 Run the three hub checks. Verify: `for h in sk-doc sk-design system-deep-loop; do node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/$h > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"$h exit=$?\"; done` prints `exit=0` three times.\n91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n92: - [ ] T034 Check scope and comment hygiene. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` names only files in `spec.md` section 3, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- '*.ts' '*.cjs' '*.mjs' '*.sh' | rg \"^\\+.*(REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|specs/|ADR-)\"` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T035 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n99: ## Completion Criteria\n100: \n101: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n102: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n103: - [ ] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 with the bullet in place\n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n109: ## Cross-References\n110: \n111: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n112: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n113: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n114: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md` R5, R6, R10b, L4, L5, L10, G1 and G3\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## Verification Checklist\n120: \n121: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n122: ## Verification Protocol\n123: \n124: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n125: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n126: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n127: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n128: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n129: \n130: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. An A6 reading above 16384 blocks the phase.\n131: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n136: ## Pre-Implementation\n137: \n138: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The four wording questions have an operator answer, quoted in `spec.md` section 10. Evidence: answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog. T003, T006, T012, T013, T015 and T026 follow those answers.\n139: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n140: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n146: ## Code Quality\n147: \n148: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] In `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `node --check` exits 0 on `SYNC` and `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n149: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n150: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n151: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n157: ## Testing Checklist\n158: \n159: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n160: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n161: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The child render test covers every renderer axis in `plan.md` (T023).\n162: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The spec gate test, the parity test and `npm test` in `$ADV` report 0 failed (T030, T031).\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n168: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n169: \n170: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: one rule, read by seven runtimes through four surfaces.\n171: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the pointer generator is checked: `rg -l \"sync-gate1-pointers\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists only files this phase changed or confirmed unchanged in `plan.md`.\n172: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` is checked: `rg -n \"GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists the core, its test and the injection contract, which names it without quoting it.\n173: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` are listed in the two test file headers.\n174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n175: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n181: ## Security\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] A child never sees a bare `start` or `ask` command line (T023).\n184: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No changed file names `/local-skilled-alignment`: `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n185: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The pointer block copies tracked `AGENTS.md` text only (T004).\n186: - [ ] CHK-033 [P0] A stored record carrying `copilot` is skipped by both readers without an error, and tool input carrying it is rejected (T022).\n187: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n192: ## Documentation\n193: \n194: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same bullet text, byte count and pin count.\n195: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] `HOOKDOC` names seven adapters and holds the invocation table (T005, T018).\n196: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The runtime-mirrors README names both pointer blocks (T021).\n197: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n198: \n199: ---\n200: \n201: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n202: ## File Organization\n203: \n204: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, before and after output live in `scratch/` only.\n205: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n206: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n211: ## Verification Summary\n212: \n213: | Category | Total | Verified |\n214: |----------|-------|----------|\n215: | P0 Items | 13 | 1/13 |\n216: | P1 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n217: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n218: \n219: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n221: \n222: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532161425,"end":1794532161960}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794532163782,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","part":{"id":"prt_1d273c0c6001oE197UwvYKrl0x","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","messageID":"msg_1d2738110001N97DJQRuDjJbBL","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"89c322dcaf7bfb964f132dda20605b03924982d3","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":10817,"output":109,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":6784,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794532170934,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","part":{"id":"prt_1d273dcb6001g9spOcWfN5VaRM","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","messageID":"msg_1d273c0cd00174bK2Bufhm7wF3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"653d5b92af7f564883b9ec5a47d53881362db1c6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532173535,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d273e552002IJAKccutrQov5X","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","messageID":"msg_1d273c0cd00174bK2Bufhm7wF3","type":"tool","id":"call_e76eb7500e0b4e2b96e343f1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 1-236\n1: ---\n2: title: Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n3: description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt; advisory only and fail-open.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor hook reference\"\n6:   - \"native-first advisor hooks\"\n7:   - \"advisor hook runtime matrix\"\n8:   - \"opencode plugin bridge\"\n9:   - \"advisor hook smoke tests\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 3.6.6.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: The Skill Advisor concern surfaces prompt-safe routing context at the moment a user submits a prompt: it scores the prompt against the maintained skill graph and, when a match clears the confidence threshold, injects a brief recommending the matching skill(s). The brief is advisory: it never replaces explicit skill loading, never persists raw prompt text, and never blocks the prompt on an advisor failure.\n22: \n23: The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n24: \n25: The single most important property is that it **fails open**: the prompt always proceeds. When the advisor call times out, fails or finds no route, the handler and the OpenCode plugin emit the directives fallback instead of a brief. An unparseable payload, an unhandled error or a shim that cannot relay its child resolves to `{}`. Every adapter honors the `skill-advisor` kill-switch, default-on.\n26: \n27: Paths beginning with `runtime/` in the package-local tables resolve from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/` (for the shims) or `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/` (for the advisor). Paths beginning with `.skilled/` are repository-root relative.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. WHAT IT DOES\n32: \n33: On each user-prompt event the adapter:\n34: \n35: 1. **Kill-switch.** Checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` (master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` or the `skill-advisor` family). Disabled → empty/skipped prompt-safe output.\n36: 2. **Read the prompt + workspace.** Resolves the workspace root (install-anchored walk, not CWD-relative, so the hook stays correct off-root), reads the prompt text (bounded), and resolves the session id.\n37: 3. **Prompt gate.** `skippedAdvisorResultFor` uses `shouldFireAdvisor` to decline skip commands, short acknowledgements and prompts below its length threshold. A declined prompt returns a skipped result and does not spawn the CLI.\n38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n39: 5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n40: 6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n41: 7. **Emit.** Native adapters emit a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON envelope. OpenCode appends to `output.system` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`. Pi sends a model-visible message.\n42: \n43: The injected brief begins with `Advisor:` and names the routed skill or, when the recommendation resolves to a command, the skill that owns it and the runnable command. A doctor command appears as its runnable `/doctor:` string on the top line or under a skill as an `Also:` second line. The handler returns `{}` when the hook is disabled, input cannot be parsed or an unhandled exception occurs. A shim also returns `{}` when it cannot resolve or relay valid child output, including on timeout. When the handler has no brief, it emits the directives fallback.\n44: \n45: ### Brief head form\n46: \n47: A recommendation that resolves to a command renders one label, shared by the `use` and `ambiguous` heads:\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: <ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The recommendation's own `ownerSkillId`, `command` and `policy` are authoritative, and the generated command row fills only what they omit. The policy parenthesis is dropped when no policy is known. A recommendation with no command row keeps its skill label rather than a command label.\n54: \n55: The `use` head reads `Advisor: <freshness>; use <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` For example:\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: ### Degraded contract\n64: \n65: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n66: \n67: - A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68: - Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n69: \n70: Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n75: \n76: Every native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n77: \n78: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n79: |---|---|---|---|---|\n80: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n81: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n82: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n83: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n84: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n85: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n86: | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n87: \n88: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n93: \n94: ```text\n95: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n96: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n97: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n98: +-- claude/\n99: |   +-- README.md\n100: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n101: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n102: +-- dsh/\n103: |   +-- README.md\n104: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n105: +-- pi/\n106: |   +-- README.md\n107: |   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n108: `-- lib/\n109:     +-- README.md\n110:     +-- directive-lifecycle.ts, directive-lifecycle-contract.ts, directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts\n111:     +-- directive-lifecycle-store.py, directive-lifecycle-vectors.json\n112:     `-- skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts\n113: \n114: system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.{ts,js}  # thin shims (claude/codex/cursor/devin)\n115: system-skill-advisor/runtime/\n116: +-- dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js   # compiled advisor the shims spawn\n117: +-- lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts, render.ts, metrics.ts, subprocess.ts\n118: `-- scripts/skill_advisor.py                      # standalone Python advisor CLI\n119: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js         # OpenCode plugin\n120: ```\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 5. KEY FILES\n125: \n126: | File | Responsibility |\n127: |---|---|\n128: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n129: | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Thin process-boundary shims. Resolve the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor, spawn the compiled advisor with bounded stdin/stdio/timeout, and relay its stdout (or `{}` on any failure). |\n130: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n131: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n132: | `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` | The CLI front door the OpenCode plugin spawns. Receives the `advisor_recommend` command line, returns the JSON payload on stdout. |\n133: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts` | The brief builder: scoring, freshness, status, confidence/uncertainty. |\n134: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | `renderAdvisorBrief` / `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`, produces the model-visible text. |\n135: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n136: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n137: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Standalone Python advisor CLI. The advisor CLI runs it as the local scorer when the daemon is unreachable. The hook never calls it directly. |\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: ## 6. CONFIGURATION\n142: \n143: The advisor is enabled by default. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive) for the shared resolver.\n144: \n145: | Variable | Effect |\n146: |---|---|\n147: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Canonical kill-switch. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output. |\n148: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters. |\n149: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the OpenCode plugin. |\n150: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n151: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the OpenCode plugin. |\n152: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n153: \n154: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (compiled-route summary bounding).\n155: \n156: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n157: \n158: ---\n159: \n160: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n161: \n162: | Boundary | Rule |\n163: |---|---|\n164: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n165: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n166: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n167: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n168: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n169: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n170: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n171: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n172: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n173: \n174: ### Operator freshness states\n175: \n176: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n177: | --- | --- | --- |\n178: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n179: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n180: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n181: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n182: \n183: ---\n184: \n185: ## 8. VALIDATION\n186: \n187: Build both maintained packages:\n188: \n189: ```bash\n190: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build\n191: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n192: ```\n193: \n194: Expected result: both builds succeed and `dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js` are produced.\n195: \n196: ```bash\n197: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck\n198: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n199: node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\n200: ```\n201: \n202: Expected result: no type errors. All advisor package tests pass. The OpenCode plugin test passes.\n203: \n204: Native smoke tests (each targets an existing compiled file):\n205: \n206: ```bash\n207: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"update documentation with DQI checks\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\"}' | \\\n208:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n209: ```\n210: \n211: Expected: `{}` or `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` beginning with `Advisor:`. Repeat for the `codex`, `cursor`, and `devin` siblings.\n212: \n213: OpenCode plugin CLI smoke test:\n214: \n215: ```bash\n216: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"save this conversation context to memory\",\"options\":{\"topK\":3,\"includeAttribution\":false,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true,\"confidenceThreshold\":0.8,\"uncertaintyThreshold\":0.35}}' \\\n217:   | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json\n218: ```\n219: \n220: Installation drift check (from a linked worktree with the required worktree flag):\n221: \n222: ```bash\n223: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree\n224: ```\n225: \n226: This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n227: \n228: ---\n229: \n230: ## 9. RELATED\n231: \n232: - [`skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`](skill-advisor-hook-validation.md): validation and audit detail for this concern.\n233: - [`claude/README.md`](claude/README.md), [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md), [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md): per-surface detail.\n234: - [`../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md`](../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md): the owning skill's hook contract (where the shims live).\n235: - [`../../../hooks/README.md`](../../../hooks/README.md): the unified hooks tree with the kill-switch index and coverage matrix.\n236: - [`../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md`](../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md): the OpenCode plugins folder that loads `system-skill-advisor.js`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 1-236\n1: ---\n2: title: Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n3: description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt; advisory only and fail-open.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor hook reference\"\n6:   - \"native-first advisor hooks\"\n7:   - \"advisor hook runtime matrix\"\n8:   - \"opencode plugin bridge\"\n9:   - \"advisor hook smoke tests\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 3.6.6.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: The Skill Advisor concern surfaces prompt-safe routing context at the moment a user submits a prompt: it scores the prompt against the maintained skill graph and, when a match clears the confidence threshold, injects a brief recommending the matching skill(s). The brief is advisory: it never replaces explicit skill loading, never persists raw prompt text, and never blocks the prompt on an advisor failure.\n22: \n23: The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n24: \n25: The single most important property is that it **fails open**: the prompt always proceeds. When the advisor call times out, fails or finds no route, the handler and the OpenCode plugin emit the directives fallback instead of a brief. An unparseable payload, an unhandled error or a shim that cannot relay its child resolves to `{}`. Every adapter honors the `skill-advisor` kill-switch, default-on.\n26: \n27: Paths beginning with `runtime/` in the package-local tables resolve from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/` (for the shims) or `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/` (for the advisor). Paths beginning with `.skilled/` are repository-root relative.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. WHAT IT DOES\n32: \n33: On each user-prompt event the adapter:\n34: \n35: 1. **Kill-switch.** Checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` (master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` or the `skill-advisor` family). Disabled → empty/skipped prompt-safe output.\n36: 2. **Read the prompt + workspace.** Resolves the workspace root (install-anchored walk, not CWD-relative, so the hook stays correct off-root), reads the prompt text (bounded), and resolves the session id.\n37: 3. **Prompt gate.** `skippedAdvisorResultFor` uses `shouldFireAdvisor` to decline skip commands, short acknowledgements and prompts below its length threshold. A declined prompt returns a skipped result and does not spawn the CLI.\n38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n39: 5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n40: 6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n41: 7. **Emit.** Native adapters emit a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON envelope. OpenCode appends to `output.system` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`. Pi sends a model-visible message.\n42: \n43: The injected brief begins with `Advisor:` and names the routed skill or, when the recommendation resolves to a command, the skill that owns it and the runnable command. A doctor command appears as its runnable `/doctor:` string on the top line or under a skill as an `Also:` second line. The handler returns `{}` when the hook is disabled, input cannot be parsed or an unhandled exception occurs. A shim also returns `{}` when it cannot resolve or relay valid child output, including on timeout. When the handler has no brief, it emits the directives fallback.\n44: \n45: ### Brief head form\n46: \n47: A recommendation that resolves to a command renders one label, shared by the `use` and `ambiguous` heads:\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: <ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The recommendation's own `ownerSkillId`, `command` and `policy` are authoritative, and the generated command row fills only what they omit. The policy parenthesis is dropped when no policy is known. A recommendation with no command row keeps its skill label rather than a command label.\n54: \n55: The `use` head reads `Advisor: <freshness>; use <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` For example:\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: ### Degraded contract\n64: \n65: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n66: \n67: - A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68: - Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n69: \n70: Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n75: \n76: Every native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n77: \n78: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n79: |---|---|---|---|---|\n80: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n81: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n82: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n83: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n84: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n85: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n86: | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n87: \n88: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n93: \n94: ```text\n95: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n96: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n97: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n98: +-- claude/\n99: |   +-- README.md\n100: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n101: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n102: +-- dsh/\n103: |   +-- README.md\n104: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n105: +-- pi/\n106: |   +-- README.md\n107: |   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n108: `-- lib/\n109:     +-- README.md\n110:     +-- directive-lifecycle.ts, directive-lifecycle-contract.ts, directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts\n111:     +-- directive-lifecycle-store.py, directive-lifecycle-vectors.json\n112:     `-- skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts\n113: \n114: system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.{ts,js}  # thin shims (claude/codex/cursor/devin)\n115: system-skill-advisor/runtime/\n116: +-- dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js   # compiled advisor the shims spawn\n117: +-- lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts, render.ts, metrics.ts, subprocess.ts\n118: `-- scripts/skill_advisor.py                      # standalone Python advisor CLI\n119: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js         # OpenCode plugin\n120: ```\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 5. KEY FILES\n125: \n126: | File | Responsibility |\n127: |---|---|\n128: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n129: | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Thin process-boundary shims. Resolve the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor, spawn the compiled advisor with bounded stdin/stdio/timeout, and relay its stdout (or `{}` on any failure). |\n130: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n131: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n132: | `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` | The CLI front door the OpenCode plugin spawns. Receives the `advisor_recommend` command line, returns the JSON payload on stdout. |\n133: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts` | The brief builder: scoring, freshness, status, confidence/uncertainty. |\n134: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | `renderAdvisorBrief` / `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`, produces the model-visible text. |\n135: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n136: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n137: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Standalone Python advisor CLI. The advisor CLI runs it as the local scorer when the daemon is unreachable. The hook never calls it directly. |\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: ## 6. CONFIGURATION\n142: \n143: The advisor is enabled by default. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive) for the shared resolver.\n144: \n145: | Variable | Effect |\n146: |---|---|\n147: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Canonical kill-switch. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output. |\n148: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters. |\n149: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the OpenCode plugin. |\n150: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n151: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the OpenCode plugin. |\n152: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n153: \n154: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (compiled-route summary bounding).\n155: \n156: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n157: \n158: ---\n159: \n160: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n161: \n162: | Boundary | Rule |\n163: |---|---|\n164: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n165: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n166: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n167: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n168: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n169: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n170: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n171: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n172: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n173: \n174: ### Operator freshness states\n175: \n176: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n177: | --- | --- | --- |\n178: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n179: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n180: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n181: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n182: \n183: ---\n184: \n185: ## 8. VALIDATION\n186: \n187: Build both maintained packages:\n188: \n189: ```bash\n190: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build\n191: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n192: ```\n193: \n194: Expected result: both builds succeed and `dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js` are produced.\n195: \n196: ```bash\n197: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck\n198: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n199: node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\n200: ```\n201: \n202: Expected result: no type errors. All advisor package tests pass. The OpenCode plugin test passes.\n203: \n204: Native smoke tests (each targets an existing compiled file):\n205: \n206: ```bash\n207: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"update documentation with DQI checks\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\"}' | \\\n208:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n209: ```\n210: \n211: Expected: `{}` or `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` beginning with `Advisor:`. Repeat for the `codex`, `cursor`, and `devin` siblings.\n212: \n213: OpenCode plugin CLI smoke test:\n214: \n215: ```bash\n216: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"save this conversation context to memory\",\"options\":{\"topK\":3,\"includeAttribution\":false,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true,\"confidenceThreshold\":0.8,\"uncertaintyThreshold\":0.35}}' \\\n217:   | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json\n218: ```\n219: \n220: Installation drift check (from a linked worktree with the required worktree flag):\n221: \n222: ```bash\n223: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree\n224: ```\n225: \n226: This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n227: \n228: ---\n229: \n230: ## 9. RELATED\n231: \n232: - [`skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`](skill-advisor-hook-validation.md): validation and audit detail for this concern.\n233: - [`claude/README.md`](claude/README.md), [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md), [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md): per-surface detail.\n234: - [`../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md`](../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md): the owning skill's hook contract (where the shims live).\n235: - [`../../../hooks/README.md`](../../../hooks/README.md): the unified hooks tree with the kill-switch index and coverage matrix.\n236: - [`../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md`](../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md): the OpenCode plugins folder that loads `system-skill-advisor.js`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532173138,"end":1794532173535}}}}
