{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532224245,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2749edb002hosuLoTY3n1FEa","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","messageID":"msg_1d2749a21001xWyJMlocJClXDh","type":"tool","id":"call_b3eec1168e9840adbbf87893","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","oldString":"OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE","newString":"OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n\n### Starting a surfaced command\n\nThe document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n\n| Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\n| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n| Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n| OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\n| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n@@ -86,8 +86,22 @@\n | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n \n OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n \n+### Starting a surfaced command\n+\n+The document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n+\n+| Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\n+| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n+| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n+| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n+| Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n+| OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\n+| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n+\n ---\n \n ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n \n","status":"modified","additions":14,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"oldString\":\"OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\",\"newString\":\"OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\\n\\n### Starting a surfaced command\\n\\nThe document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\\n\\n| Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\\n| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\\n| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\\n| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\\n| Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\\n| OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\\n| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532220635,"end":1794532224245}}}}
