{"type":"text","timestamp":1794532249786,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","part":{"id":"prt_1d27506fe002l1xs5lwzglXY1L","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e4f65ffeV4WrEmvaY5YjgO","messageID":"msg_1d274ef07001NWKu1h8gqhoh3a","type":"text","text":"T018 complete.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` — appended `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3 (14 added lines), with the command-document prose and a three-column per-runtime table in plain-text runtime names, including the Claude Code Skill-tool row. No other edits: T005's DSH row/directory entry show in the working-tree diff but were untouched by me. Checkbox in `tasks.md` left unticked.\n\n**Verify output** (run from repository root)\n```\n$ HOOKDOC=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n$ rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" \"$HOOKDOC\"\n90:### Starting a surfaced command\n$ rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' \"$HOOKDOC\"\n7\n```\nBoth conditions hold: exactly 1 heading line and the adapter-table bold-row count is still 7.\n\n**Not done / notes**\n- No failures, nothing blocked.\n- The only judgment calls: row order follows the task's listed order (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode, DSH), and the Basis cells condense section 2.8's evidence, including its \"public docs not fetched\" caveats for Cursor and Pi.","time":{"start":1794532247294,"end":1794532249786}}}
